== Notes ==

* The "-2 morale check" is applied separately from the frightened status, and consequently is not removed by remove fear, nor blocked by [[mind-affecting]] immunity. Due to a bug, if the target is immune to fear these penalties will be applied automatically without a saving throw.
* The penalty to saving throws is only for will saves versus mind-affecting, but does not stack with the -2 penalty to all saving throws inherent to the frightened status.
* The penalty to damage rolls only reduces [[magical damage]]. If the affected creature does not deal magical damage in its attacks, there will be no change to the damage dealt.
* This spell is actually an implementation of the [[pencil-and-paper]] [[Dungeons & Dragons]] spell ''cause fear''. In pencil-and-paper, ''[[scare (grimoire)|scare]]'' is a second level version of this spell, with an [[area of effect]] affecting multiple targets.
*Due to a .2da bug, ''scare'' is not an additional [[counterspell]] of ''remove fear''.
*There is an inconsistent resref/TAG naming anomaly as a spell scroll. ResRef and TAG naming use 2, but wizard/sorcerer spell level is 1. This difference affects on random loot generation, because this spell scroll longer available to HD 10. (Normally wizard/sorcerer spell level 1 available only to HD 8.)

